   "question": "The claim: the 220 um f-P0.10 fiber PENG delivers a maximum 136.9 uW at 10 MOhm load, 6.5x the cast-film PENG. Cross-checking panels F7d (load-dependent voltage) and F7b (open-circuit voltage) for this same device, does the data across the two panels support this claim?",
   "answer_key": "No. Cross-checking the two panels for the same 220 um f-P0.10 device shows an inconsistency: the load-voltage plateau in F7d reaches about 83 V, which exceeds the 62 V open-circuit voltage peak for that device shown in F7b. A load voltage cannot legitimately exceed the open-circuit voltage of the same device, so this cross-check does not support the claim as read from the panels.",
   "answer_scope": "full",
   "grading": "Answer key: the audit ruling on the panel, node o24, which reports the load-voltage plateau (~83 V, F7d) exceeding the 62 V open-circuit peak (F7b) for the same 220 um f-P0.10 device.",
